{"id": "R7", "severity": "major", "adrs": ["ADR-0006", "ADR-0010", "ADR-0001"], "text": "`SaveHost` has no legal home. ADR-0006 diagram and �1.5: 'SaveHost (Node, PROCESS_MODE_ALWAYS, priority 0)' with `_process` polling. ADR-0006 puts files in `src/<save module>/`. ADR-0010 �1.1 says `src/save/` has no Node-derived classes, �4.1/SIM-01 ban `Node` and `_process` in L0 to L2 with no waiver, and `src/game/` is described as holding only the composition root, `KernelHost`, `MonotonicClock`, boot walks and dev loaders. SaveHost is not placed anywhere. ADR-0006 OQ-F also doubts that a priority-0 poll gives tick-boundary semantics. A priority-0 node is also a third PRESENTATION-level node (KRN-03/KRN-05 walk) that no ADR accounts for."}
---
{"id": "R8", "severity": "major", "adrs": ["ADR-0006", "ADR-0010"], "text": "Wall-clock needs of Save/Load collide with the clock lint. ADR-0006 �1.12 keeps `created_unix` in the header as 'metadata', and `SaveInfo`/list_saves need a displayable time. ADR-0010 �4.5 SIM-02 bans `Time.get_unix_time_from_system`/`get_datetime_dict_from_system` in all of `src/` outside `kernel_host.gd`, the diagnostics timer and `monotonic_clock.gd`. The `Clock` port is 'Monotonic microseconds ... Never wall time'. ADR-0006's millisecond timeouts can use `Clock`, but `created_unix` has no sanctioned source (ADR-0010 OQ-D already notes MonotonicClock is not in ADR-0001's allow-list). ADR-0005 �1.7 meanwhile allows 'render-time timers in Adapter/Presenter (TR-pc-027)', which SIM-02 does not."}
---
{"id": "R9", "severity": "major", "adrs": ["ADR-0006", "ADR-0002", "ADR-0005"], "text": "ControlHandle shape and snapshot outcome do not match ADR-0002. ADR-0006 writes `ControlHandle.request_snapshot() -> ControlOutcome{payload: Dictionary (deep copy)}` as if synchronous. ADR-0002 Key Interfaces: `func request_snapshot() -> void`, with the outcome delivered via `set_outcome_handler(handler)` at the per-frame flush, and the outcome carrying only `request_kind, outcome, tick` plus the payload for a snapshot. ADR-0006 �3 and ADR-0005 Related need the kernel to supply `T`, `state_hash(PERSIST,T)`, each block's `block_hash`/`enc_len` at capture ('the kernel supplies each block's block_hash, enc_len and the state_hash'), but ADR-0002's ControlOutcome has no such fields. `expected_state_hash`: ADR-0006 passes `Variant` with null meaning 'no verdict' (its OQ-B); ADR-0002 and the registry have `expected_state_hash: int = 0`, and 0 is a legal H64 value."}
---
{"id": "R10", "severity": "minor", "adrs": ["ADR-0006", "ADR-0005", "ADR-0004"], "text": "ADR-0006 �1.9 mitigation rung 1 ('the kernel skips `snapshot()` for a block whose cached hash (ADR-0005) is unchanged ... needs ADR-0004's debug check that every changed block marked a dirty key') contradicts both siblings. ADR-0005 �5.4 lists 'the snapshot capture' as an always-uncached path and the cache as diagnostics-only. ADR-0004 �7 says a dirty key cannot gate caching (quantised writes mark nothing) and its audit explicitly excludes `quiet_writes_allowed` blocks; the sound input is the touch serial. Related: ADR-0005's Related cites ADR-0006's `block_state_hash`, but ADR-0006 never uses that name ('per-block hashes')."}
---
{"id": "R11", "severity": "minor", "adrs": ["ADR-0006", "ADR-0005"], "text": "Duplicate and divergent 64-bit hex codecs. ADR-0006 defines `SaveCodec.hex64_to_int/int_to_hex64` (hex_decode plus size check) while ADR-0005 owns `Hex64.encode/decode` (src/shared/det) and says `hex_decode` accepts uppercase (P16) so it validates exactly 16 lowercase `[0-9a-f]` first. ADR-0006 �1.3 requires 'lowercase' but its decode rule has no lowercase check. ADR-0010 lets `save` import `shared`, so the duplication is avoidable. ADR-0006 �1.1/OQ-I also assumes a Graph `canonical_bytes()` embedded as a `PackedByteArray` snapshot field, but ADR-0005 �3.1 removes owner `canonical_bytes()` entirely (the kernel encodes the snapshot payload)."}
---
{"id": "R12", "severity": "minor", "adrs": ["ADR-0004", "ADR-0006"], "text": "The Save/Load trigger path is left open on both sides. ADR-0004 OQ-3: Save/Load is a host service with no CR-10 class; 'recommended: poll an owner read view', and if a subscription is wanted 'ADR-0006 or ADR-0009 names the class'. ADR-0006 says Save/Load is 'a control-plane caller, not a subscriber' and its OQ-F asks 'whether ADR-0004 should offer a control-plane end-of-tick callback'. ADR-0009 names no class. Neither provides the mechanism for the POD_ARRIVED/BERTHED autosave triggers."}
---
{"id": "R14", "severity": "major", "adrs": ["ADR-0001", "ADR-0002", "ADR-0003", "ADR-0004", "ADR-0005", "ADR-0006", "ADR-0008", "ADR-0009"], "text": "None of the amendments the new ADRs request has been applied to ADR-0001/0002/0003 (grep over those three files finds none of these identifiers): `Kernel.deliver_frame_end()` as the last step of `TickDriver.frame` (ADR-0004); `NotifyFacet`, `BlockRegistrar.register_key_space`, `WriteScope.emit_event`, `SUBSCRIBE_REFUSED`/`DIRTY_KEY_INVALID`/`DIRTY_KEY_KIND_UNDECLARED`/`EVENT_OVERFLOW`/`MISSED_DIRTY_MARK` and the touch serial on the H1 allow-list (ADR-0004); `ModuleFacet.rng`, `WriteScope.has_opened`, and `kernel.clock` carrying `(T, world_seed, restore_epoch)` (ADR-0005 attributes restore_epoch to ADR-0001, which never mentions it; ADR-0006 �3.5 expects a kernel.clock view entry); `PresentationClock.load_seq` (ADR-0009); `ProcessPriority.PRESENTATION_LATE` (ADR-0008 OQ-D); a kernel-state accessor (ADR-0008). ADR-0003 still says 'key is an opaque int; its layout is ADR-0004's'. Acceptance of ADR-0004/5/8/9 is gated on these."}
---
{"id": "R15", "severity": "minor", "adrs": ["ADR-0004", "ADR-0005", "ADR-0006", "ADR-0008", "ADR-0009", "ADR-0010"], "text": "docs/registry/architecture.yaml is unchanged (last_updated 2026-10-28) and has no entry citing ADR-0004/5/6/8/9/10; every ADR defers its registry candidates to the orchestrator. Existing entries are now incomplete against them: `block_registration` signature lacks `register_key_space`; `presentation_clock` lacks `load_seq`; `control_plane` signature lacks types and the outcome-handler shape; `frame_order` lacks `PRESENTATION_LATE`; no state_ownership entries for `touch_serial`, `restore_epoch` (three owners are implied: Save/Load slot_epoch.bin per ADR-0006 �3.1, kernel.clock view, RngFacet derivation), `present_time` (PipelineRoot) or `load_seq`; no `api_decisions` for the notify transport. Registry fault_domain_table says domains 15-31 are presentation/tooling, but ADR-0008 OQ-E asks whether the pipeline needs one and ADR-0010 (named co-decider) does not answer."}
---
{"id": "R18", "severity": "minor", "adrs": ["ADR-0004", "ADR-0005", "ADR-0006", "ADR-0008", "ADR-0009", "ADR-0010", "ADR-0007"], "text": "Dependency and ordering tables are stale or asymmetric. ADR-0009 Depends On lists ADR-0001/2/3 only, yet its own Ordering Note says Acceptance requires ADR-0004 Accepted and it consumes ADR-0008's `present_time` and `frame_pre_draw`; ADR-0008 and ADR-0009 each list the other under Enables but neither depends on the other; ADR-0004 and ADR-0010 each list the other under Enables; ADR-0008 Depends On omits ADR-0007 (RenderTuning, ZOOM_MIN_K) and ADR-0006 (DisplaySettings persistence). Ordering Notes in ADR-0008 and ADR-0010 still call ADR-0004/5/6/8/9 'not yet written'; ADR-0010 SIM-13 is 'a slot until ADR-0004 is written' although ADR-0004 now decides the registry transport and ADR-0009 �8 agrees. ADR-0010 matrix gives `save` no edge to `data`, but ADR-0006 depends on ADR-0007 for `catalogue_version` and Save/Load's tuning table, which ADR-0007 injects through setup() (`RegistryView`/`BuildConstants` are also unplaced)."}
---

